Sure! Below is a minimal example of an “interactive card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML + CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body{
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card{
    width:260px;          /* width of the card */
    height:360px;         /* height of the card */
    perspective:800px;    /* gives depth to the 3D transform */
    cursor:pointer;       /* hand icon on hover */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner wrapper ---------- */
.card-inner{
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform .6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;     /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner{
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* rotate 180° around Y‑axis */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face{
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card-front{
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    color:#333;
}

.card-back{
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* place back face opposite front */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    color:#555;
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣ Sample content ---------- */
.card-front img{
    width:80%;
    border-radius:8px;
    margin-bottom:12px;
}
.card-front h3{
    margin:0;
    font-size:1.4rem;
}
.card-back p{
    padding:0 20px;
    text-align:center;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/150?random=1" alt="Sample image">
            <h3>Front Title</h3>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <p>This is the back side of the card. Hover again to flip back.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| 1 | Basic page styling – center the card vertically & horizontally. |
| 2 | `.card` sets the *perspective* so that 3D transforms look realistic. |
| 3 | `.card-inner` holds both faces and has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its children stay in 3D space. |
| 4 | On hover we rotate `.card-inner` 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| 5 | Each face (`.card-face`) is absolutely positioned and has `backface-visibility:hidden` so the hidden side disappears during rotation. |
| 6 | Sample content – you can replace the image, titles, or text with your own. |

Feel free to tweak the dimensions, colors, or add more content. If you need a different rotation axis (e.g., X‑axis) just change `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` (or any other angle). Enjoy!
